{
  "_help": "EXPERIMENTAL: first guesses, not tested in every game. Tune them and send improvements. Trigger travel has zones 0 (rest) to 9 (fully pressed). Most Xbox games register a trigger press at about zone 1 (XInput threshold 30/255), so clicks and snaps are placed early to land when the game reacts. Modes: off | feedback {start 0-9, strength 1-8} | slope {start, end, start_strength, end_strength} | multi {strengths: 10 values 0-8} | weapon {start 2-7, end, strength} | bow {start 0-7, end, strength, snap} | vibration {start, amplitude 1-8, frequency Hz} | machine {start, end, amplitude_a 0-7, amplitude_b 0-7, frequency, period} | galloping {start, end, first_foot 0-6, second_foot, frequency}. A game uses a preset ('preset': 'name') and may override L2 or R2. Games with '_native_dualsense': true have their own effects: play those with Xbox mode off. '_exe' lists the game's .exe names for automatic switching (best effort; use 'Remember for this game' in the app for anything missing).",
  "_native_exe": {"_note": "Games with their own DualSense support: Xbox mode is switched OFF when they come to the front.", "list": ["cyberpunk2077.exe", "gow.exe", "godofwar.exe", "spider-man.exe", "milesmorales.exe", "riftapart.exe", "tlou-i.exe", "horizonforbiddenwest.exe", "ghostoftsushima.exe", "ds.exe", "returnal-win64-shipping.exe", "shproto-win64-shipping.exe"]},
